      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will usually suppress the sheaf of rings <MATH_0001>\nin the notation when discussing locally ringed spaces. We will\nsimply refer to ``the locally ringed space <MATH_0002>''.\nWe will by abuse of notation think of <MATH_0003> also as\nthe underlying topological space. Finally we will denote\nthe corresponding sheaf of rings\n<MATH_0004> as the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>structure sheaf of <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\nIn addition, it is customary to denote the maximal ideal\nof the local ring <MATH_0006> by\n<MATH_0007> or simply <MATH_0008>.\nWe will say ``let <MATH_0009> be a morphism of locally ringed\nspaces'' thereby suppressing the structure sheaves even further.\nIn this case, we will by abuse of notation think of <MATH_0010>\nalso as the underlying continuous map of topological spaces.\nThe <MATH_0011>-map corresponding to <MATH_0012> will customarily\nbe denoted <MATH_0013>. The condition that <MATH_0014> is a morphism\nof locally ringed spaces can then be expressed by saying that\nfor every <MATH_0015> the map on stalks\n<MATH_0016>\nmaps the maximal ideal <MATH_0017> into\n<MATH_0018>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet us use these notational conventions to show that the\ncollection of locally ringed spaces and morphisms of locally\nringed spaces forms a category. In order to see this we have\nto show that the composition of morphisms of locally ringed\nspaces is a morphism of locally ringed spaces. OK, so let\n<MATH_0019> and <MATH_0020> be morphism of locally\nringed spaces. The composition of <MATH_0021> and <MATH_0022> is defined in\nSheaves, Definition <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0023>. By\nSheaves, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthe composition\n<MATH_0024>\nis the associated map on stalks for the morphism <MATH_0025>.\nThe result follows since a composition of local ring\nhomomorphisms is a local ring homomorphism.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nA pleasing feature of the definition is the fact that the functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>Locally ringed spaces<MATHSEG_0002>Ringed spaces<MATHSEG_0003>\nreflects isomorphisms (plus more).\nHere is a less abstract statement.\n\n",
      "source_status": "CURRENT",
